{"type":"npc","name":"Vengeful Doormat","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":24,"temp":0,"max":24,"details":""},"ac":{"value":15,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":15,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":"mudstrider"}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common"],"details":"Can't speak any language"},"level":{"value":1},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Animated by their sheer hatred of being trodden on every day, these doormats have had <em>enough</em> of being wiped with dirty feet. They retaliate the only way they know how: by subjecting their targets to mud, filth, and endless stomping. The magic that gives these carpets a spark of life also increases their size, allowing them to wrap fully around and crush their original owners. Only legless creatures like snakes and worms are spared from the vengeful doormats' wrath.</p><p>Vengeful doormats typically arise in rural towns, where muddy boots are commonplace. Such doormats are a nuisance, but locals can band together to deal with them. However, gigantic doormats found in mansions and castles can be a truly fearsome force, requiring trained combatants and cleaning crews to slay them. Some truly cruel rug makers purposefully spawn these creatures, selling their corpses to nobles looking for a status symbol and still-animated doormats to sadists wanting to leave a nasty surprise at a front door.</p><p>Vengeful doormats have the amazing capability of attracting animated brooms, which then continuously dust the doormats off. Some arcane scholars theorize that animated brooms might be the key to a more ethical way to manage the vengeance of the doormats, as properly dusted doormats are markedly less aggressive.</p><p>In some cases, vengeful doormats turn back into normal doormats after achieving their retribution. This transformation typically occurs after the vengeful doormat has killed or severely maimed its original owner, but the doormat is occasionally satisfied with simply covering the owner's body and everything they treasure in mud.</p><h2>Welcome Message</h2><p>For the unwary, there aren't a lot of clues that a vengeful doormat is anything out of the ordinary. A frequent tell-tale sign of a feral doormat is that it displays an embroidered message in which it vents its rage, from a pithy \"GO AWAY!\" to a more specific message, such as \"BILL WITHERS, IF YOU WALK ACROSS THIS THRESHOLD WITH THOSE MUDDY HOBNAILED BOOTS AGAIN, SO HELP ME, I WON'T BE HELD RESPONSIBLE!\" For creatures of rather limited intellect, vengeful doormats are surprisingly good spellers.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 3.5/7/13 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Stealth, Survival)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, constitution, dexterity, earth, earth armor, energy resistant (spirit, vitality, void), sensory (darkvision), strength, throwing, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"David Metraux","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":4},"dex":{"mod":2},"con":{"mod":4},"int":{"mod":-3},"wis":{"mod":1},"cha":{"mod":1}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":4,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"tremorsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":15}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":9,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":7,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":4,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":5,"special":[]},"athletics":{"base":7,"special":[]},"stealth":{"base":7,"special":[]},"survival":{"base":4,"special":[{"label":"to Track footprints","predicate":["action:track","footprints"],"base":7}]}},"traits":{"value":["construct","earth"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"FEGVklTE5yEyBocO","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/vengeful-doormat.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Vengeful Doormat","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/vengeful-doormat.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/vengeful-doormat.webp"}},"flags":{"sf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"type":"action","name":"Dirty Retribution","system":{"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature succeeds at a melee Strike against the vengeful doormat</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The doormat angrily summons forth and flings dirt at the offending creature, attempting to disgust it. The creature must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:15] save or be @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 1}.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["arcane","earth"]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"dXriEYNL0nZfwJdF","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Foot Vulnerability","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>A vengeful doormat takes 2 additional damage from Strikes made with feet. A creature can @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.actions.Item.PMbdMWc2QroouFGD]{Grapple} a vengeful doormat without a free hand by entering the doormat's square and stepping on it.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[{"key":"Weakness","type":"custom","value":2,"definition":[{"or":["item:slug:kick","item:slug:foot","item:slug:hoof","item:slug:dragon-tail"]}]}],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"meqtNLe6bcs8JA6m","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/OneAction.webp","name":"Grab","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"actions":{"value":1},"category":"offensive","description":{"value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Grab]</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Monster Core","authors":""},"rules":[],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"slug":"grab","_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":null}},"type":"action","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.sf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.Tkd8sH4pwFIPzqTr","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"FNdBTJR6HzsBWJGn"},{"type":"action","name":"Mud Spray","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per hour</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The vengeful doormat shakes itself off, spraying massive quantities of mud out in a @Template[type:cone|distance:15]. The muddy area is difficult terrain. The mud persists for 1 hour before reappearing on the doormat's body.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":2},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"8bUwPQABKXRX0BD4","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Unwelcome Mat","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"description":{"value":"<p>The vengeful doormat flattens and folds its body down to the ground. Until the next time it acts, the vengeful doormat appears to be a mundane doormat. It has an automatic result of 27 on Deception checks and DCs to pass as a doormat.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migr